Key Takeaways
Table
Lesson	Explanation
Encoding ≠ Encryption	Base64, hex, string reversal — all easily reversible
Never hardcode secrets	Even encoded secrets can be extracted from source
Security through obscurity fails	Hiding data with encoding chains doesn't protect it
Always verify your decode	Re-encode to confirm you got the right answer
Defense Tips
Store secrets in environment variables or secure vaults (HashiCorp Vault, AWS Secrets Manager)
Use proper hashing (bcrypt, Argon2) — not encoding
If encryption is needed, use AES-256-GCM with keys stored separately




